 company has partnerships with various companies, including hyperscalers, service providers, global system integrators, and software and hardware vendors that include Adobe, Amazon Web Services, Microsoft, Oracle, Salesforce, Samsung Electronics and SAP, and others. It also has a collaboration with Arm Holdings plc to develop new dual-architecture hardware for AI and data intensive workloads; partnership with three.ws to advance ai-powered 3d agent technology; and collaboration with Lightwell to help strengthen open source software supply chain. Additionally, it offers operational resilience, logistics, and future-ready technology to the UK Ministry of Defence through Team ORION. The company was formerly known as Computing-Tabulating-Recording Co. and changed its name to International Business Machines Corporation in 1924. International Business Machines Corporation was incorporated in 1911 and is headquartered in Armonk, New York.","employees":264300,"website":"https://www.ibm.com","country":"United States","city":"Armonk","officers":[{"name":"Mr. Arvind  Krishna","title":"CEO, President & Chairman"},{"name":"Mr. James J. Kavanaugh","title":"CFO and Senior VP of Finance & Operations"},{"name":"Ms. Anne E. Robinson","title":"Senior VP & Chief Legal Officer"}]},"sector_medians":{"fpe":18.39,"tpe":32.55,"ps":6.516,"pfcf":32.14,"peg":1.005,"pb":7.933,"rev_growth":0.215,"eps_growth":0.4515,"eps_growth_fwd":0.2552,"eps_growth_next":0.1933,"div_yield":0.0011,"roe":0.2323,"roa":0.07977,"de":47.91,"gross_margin":0.5924,"op_margin":0.225,"profit_margin":0.1914,"current_ratio":1.554},"valuation":[{"k":"fpe","label":"Forward P/E","v":19.16,"sector":18.39,"verdict":"Fairly valued"},{"k":"tpe","label":"TTM P/E","v":21.63,"sector":32.55,"verdict":"Undervalued"},{"k":"ps","label":"Price / Sales","v":3.43,"sector":6.516,"verdict":"Undervalued"},{"k":"pfcf","label":"Price / FCF","v":19.4,"sector":32.14,"verdict":"Undervalued"},{"k":"peg","label":"PEG","v":2.4,"sector":1.005,"verdict